m/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":346,"closed_issues":2304,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T09:34:58Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":8,"created_at":"2026-10-04T13:19:06Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T00:19:03Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot 4.8-dev7.mono\n\n\n### System information\n\nOS: Windows 11 Home 64-bit | CPU: Intel Core i5-13420H | RAM: 16 GB | GPU: Intel UHD Graphics |  Display: 1920×1080, 60 Hz | Type: Notebook\n\n### Issue description\n\nI am working normally on a 3D game in the Godot editor. Suddenly, a problem occurs in the 3D Viewport where the editor camera starts moving up or down by itself when I hold the left mouse button.\n\nThis is not the camera in the running game. It is the editor camera in the 3D Viewport.\n\nThe issue happens randomly, with an estimated probability of around 60%.\nbut it almost always appears after about 25 minutes.\n\nRestarting Godot completely always fixes the issue temporarily.\n(Other versions of Godot are fine, and the keyboard is too.)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open a 3D project in Godot 4.8-dev7.\n2. Switch to the 3D Viewport.\n3. Work normally with the editor camera.\n4. Hold the left mouse button.\n5. The 3D Viewport camera may suddenly start moving up or down by itself.\n6. The movement is not caused by the intended camera controls.\n7. Close and restart Godot.\n8. The issue is temporarily resolved.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nJust a heads-up: there's a mix of Czech and English.\n\nSource Code in .zip: https://homebax.itch.io/game","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https:/